"""Claude-written keyword cues for the OIICS 2.01 two-digit event codes (used by build_oiics_event.py).

They are a CONSISTENCY GUARD, not a labeller: a NEISS-Work narrative is kept only when its human-coded event
(NIOSH coders) is supported by at least one positive cue of that code and no 'strong' cue of a competing code
fires (see STRONG and the builder). Rows failing the guard are dropped, never relabelled.
Narratives are upper-case NEISS text with abbreviations (YOM = year-old male, S P = status post, DX = diagnosis,
PT = patient, C O = complains of, FB = foreign body, LAC = laceration, FX = fracture, MVC = motor-vehicle crash).
"""

